speechtext:
This is devoted to the salaries of the staff under the statistician. It is practically for part of the staff employed on the statistical year-book. The vote for that book goes to the Printing Bureau and this is to pay some of the staff who are engaged in its composition. A part of the staff are regular clerks on the civil list, and a part are paid out of this sum. They are R. E. Watts, $900 ; J. R. Monroe, $800 ; C. Ross. $700 ; J. C. H. Pelletier, $550; making a total of $2,950. The other $250 may or may not be expended, according to circumstances, in any slight extra work required.
